    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d474">

                <pb facs="1027" n="987" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p1/pg987"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">674.84A/8–2652: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 474<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Egypt (Caffery) to the Department of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d474-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-08-26T20:00:00+02:00">August 26, 1952—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>479. PriMin told me (re Deptel 368, Aug 20) this eve that his program is
                    in fol order: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>To put the internal sit straight.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>To negotiate for Middle East def.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>To reach agrmt with Israel.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>At this point I must remind Dept with emphasis that during the first winter after
                    my arrival here under Sirry Govt I was
                    able to persuade Sirry and the Palace to
                    promise to try reach agrmt with <pb facs="1028" n="988" xml:id="pg988"/> Israel
                    and that on two occasions leaks came out to Tel Aviv and the Egypts dropped the
                    whole business like a very hot brick.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d474-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d474-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to London and Tel Aviv.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
